By moving the `reserved-memory` node to the RTD129x device tree and converting the RPC memory reservations into `reserved-memory` nodes, the patch centralizes memory management for the SoCs. This ensures that the memory regions are properly reserved and accessible, eliminating the conflicts and misconfigurations that arose from the previous setup.


